==Middle English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈlɛːdən/|lang=enm}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|enm|ang|lǣdan}}, from {{inh|enm|gem-pro|*laidijaną}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|enm|lede|leaden|leeden|lædden}}

====Verb====
{{head|enm|verb}}

# to {{l|en|lead|id=guide}} {{gloss|guide, conduct, direct}}
#: '''1395''' [[w:Wycliffe bible|Wycliffe Bible]], [http://www.studylight.org/desk/index.cgi?t1=en_wyc&q1=Romans%202 Romans 2:4]
#:: Whether `dispisist thou the richessis of his goodnesse, and the pacience, and the long abidyng? Knowist thou not, that the benygnyte of God '''ledith''' thee to forthenkyng?
#: '''1395''' Wycliffe Bible, [http://www.studylight.org/desk/index.cgi?t1=en_wyc&q1=2%20Chronicles%2025 II Chronicles 25:11]
#:: Forsothe Amasie '''ledde''' out tristili his puple, and yede in to the valei of makyngis of salt, and he killide of the sones of Seir ten thousynde.
#: '''1395''' Wycliffe Bible, [http://www.studylight.org/desk/index.cgi?t1=en_wyc&q1=Isaiah%2053 Isaiah 53:7]
#:: He was offrid, for he wolde, and he openyde not his mouth; as a scheep he schal be '''led''' to sleyng, and he schal be doumb as a lomb bifore hym that clippith it, and he schal not opene his mouth.
# to {{l|en|lead}} {{gloss|manage, oversee, administrate}}
# to {{l|en|lead}} {{gloss|rule, head, hold ultimate authority}}
# to [[carry]], [[take]], [[bring]]
# to [[put]], [[place]], [[set down]]
# to {{l|en|lead}} (a life), to live
# to [[cause]], [[engender]], [[beget]]

